hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2682","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Miqdām al-'Ijlī, narrated to us Hammād, on the authority of Ayyūb, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (RA) that a man asked the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) while he was in that place, saying: \O Messenger of Allāh"," what garments may the muḥrim not wear?\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) replied: \""He should not wear shirts"," trousers"," turbans"," or leather socks"," except if he cannot find shoes"," in which case he may wear them below the ankles. He should not wear any garment that has been touched by wars (a type of yellow dye) or zaʿfaran (saffron)"," nor a quilted cloak (burnus).\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"2683","Narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, narrated to us Hushaym, who informed us Ibn 'Awn. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham, narrated to us Hushaym, from Ibn 'Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\If a person in ihram does not find sandals"," then let him wear leather socks (khufayn) and cut them below the ankles.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
